{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310812,"nonce":"+ao/dhN8MvtR2qixMFIvBVqGQWg=","title":"SsaBarrier opacity primitive landed at extern CallDirect (2026-06-07). Closes the Cranelift egraph elaboration class for extern-linkage ...","message":"- `IrInstruction::SsaBarrier { dest, src, ty }` MIR variant + C / interpreter\n  / Cranelift lowering (all three are passthrough at the instruction level\n  — the actual opacity primitive is emitted in-place at the extern\n  CallDirect handler in `cranelift_backend.rs`).\n- `Self::ssa_barrier_value(builder, value)` helper picks the opacity\n  primitive from the actual Cranelift machine type, not MIR's declared type:\n  - Float: `fadd(v, +0.0)`\n  - Int / ptr / bool: stack slot store + load\n  - Vector / ref: passthrough (unhandled; no observed regression)\n- Inserted in-place at extern CallDirect, AFTER `value_map.insert`. No new\n  IrId, no MIR-level barrier_dest. Reuses dest_reg directly.\n\n\nFirst attempt allocated `barrier_dest = alloc_reg_typed(return_ty)` and\nreturned it from `mir_builder::call()`. On aarch64, `Inst::gen_move`\nfires `assert!(to_reg.class() == from_reg.class())` because for some\nextern calls, MIR's `return_ty` is `F64` while the actual Cranelift call\nresult has machine type `I32`. Downstream consumers of `barrier_dest`\nquery the MIR type, get F64, emit float-typed instructions; underlying\nvalue is I32 → class mismatch → crash.\n\nBisect: I64-only enabled = no crash. F32/F64-only enabled = crash on the\nfirst I32 print (proving the F64-MIR-vs-I32-cranelift mismatch on extern\nreturn). The in-place approach reuses the same IrId, so MIR-level type\nqueries are unchanged.\n\n\n**Fixes (verified):**\n- Paris MATCH: \"The capital of France is Paris\" preserved at 6 tokens.\n- 128/128 haxe regression: all green.\n- Provides infrastructure for future MIR passes that need an SSA barrier.\n\n**Does NOT fix:**\n- `Sys.time()` at top of `GenerationLoop.generate` still hangs after the\n  function prints `[gen] streaming...` (Main.hx). The barrier is wrapped\n  around Sys.time's return value, but the downstream hang is at a\n  different point in lowering — likely in non-extern method calls\n  (`model.resetCache`, etc.) that follow. Different mechanism than the\n  egraph elaboration class this barrier closes.\n- See `bugs_sys_call_in_generation_method` — still open.\n\n\nThe MIR/Cranelift type mismatch (MIR says F64, Cranelift call sig\nreturns I32) is a real pre-existing issue in rayzor's lowering. It\ndoesn't trip anywhere else because no other code allocates a new IrId\nthat aliases an existing Value via passthrough. If we ever do, the\nsame class-mismatch will resurface. Worth a debug-only validator pass\nthat walks MIR and asserts `register_types[id] is compatible with\nvalue_map[id].machine_type` after Cranelift lowering finishes.\n\n\n- `compiler/src/ir/instructions.rs` — variant added\n- `compiler/src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs` — handler + `ssa_barrier_value` helper + in-place wrap at extern CallDirect\n- `compiler/src/codegen/c_backend.rs` — passthrough arm\n- `compiler/src/codegen/mir_interpreter.rs` — opcode + executor\n- `compiler/src/ir/mir_builder.rs` — call() unchanged (no MIR auto-insertion)\n- `docs/design/ssa_barrier_instruction.md` — design doc updated with landing note\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_ssa_barrier_extern_calldirect` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}